// The one lowering: checked Zen (the AST for structure, sema's published
// facts for meaning) to the one IR (gen_ir), which every backend renders.
// docs/IR_ARCHITECTURE.md §2 is the design. The work is split by concern:
//
//   gen_lower_core    frames, slots, places, statements, expressions,
//                     patterns, `.try()`, coercions, instantiation
//   gen_lower_call    calls, closures inlined where they are written,
//                     `loop`, `Ptr`, conversions, formatting, construction
//   gen_lower_member  member resolution, bound values, `Mem`, `std.sys`
//   gen_lower_shape   layouts of checked types
//
// This module is the entry point and owns the failure type. Unsupported
// reachable constructs fail here, before any artifact is published; which
// backend can render which part of the IR is that backend's `supports`
// (gen_ir_feature), not a property of the lowering.
Span = std.ast
str = std.text
lower* = gen.gen_lower_core

Fault* = { span*: Span, what*: str }
LowerError* = OutOfMemory | Unsupported(Fault)

unsupported* = (span: Span, what: str) LowerError {
    LowerError.Unsupported(Fault(span: span, what: what))
}
